MATH 10.1.5.solution_overview:
Exact Verdopplung every $T$ $2$ . $$
e^{kT} = 2\implies k = \frac{\ln 2}{T}
$$ $P(t)=P_0\,2^{t/T}$ . Integer multiples of $T$ produce exact powers of two, never a linear count of doublings. Die Aussage wird anhand der Übersicht geprüft.

